<% content_for :title, "Import Settlements" %>

<div class="page-header">
  <div class="page-title-group">
    <h1>Import Settlement Statements</h1>
    <p class="page-kicker">Upload the PDFs your carrier sends. Revenue and every deduction are read straight off them.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="action-bar">
    <%= link_to "Recorded Settlements", settlements_path, class: "btn btn-secondary" %>
  </div>
</div>

<%= form_with url: settlement_import_path, method: :post, multipart: true, class: "form-card" do %>
  <div class="form-grid">
    <div class="field">
      <%= label_tag :statements, "Settlement PDFs" %>
      <%= file_field_tag "statements[]", multiple: true, accept: "application/pdf" %>
      <p class="field-hint">
        Select as many as you like — a whole folder at once is fine. Anything already imported is
        skipped, so re-uploading the same file is harmless.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="field">
      <%= label_tag :truck_id, "Truck" %>
      <%= select_tag :truck_id,
            options_from_collection_for_select(@trucks, :id, :display_name, current_user.default_truck&.id),
            include_blank: "Use my default truck" %>
    </div>

    <label class="checkbox-field">
      <%= check_box_tag :replace_existing, "1", false %>
      Replace deductions I already entered by hand for these dates
    </label>
    <p class="field-hint">
      Leave this off the first time. Any statement that looks like it was already typed in is held
      back and reported rather than recorded twice, so you can see the overlap before deciding.
      Tick it only once you have seen that list and want the imported version to win.
    </p>

    <div class="action-bar">
      <%= submit_tag "Read Statements" %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>

<div class="note-box">
  <strong>Every statement is checked against itself.</strong> The deductions read off the page are
  added back up and compared to the Total Deductions the statement prints. Anything that does not
  match to the cent is reported and left alone rather than imported half-read.
</div>

<div class="note-box is-warning">
  <strong>If you have been entering settlements by hand, read this first.</strong> Importing a
  statement you already typed in would record the same deductions twice. Any statement that overlaps
  what is already on your books is held back and listed, and nothing is written until you say which
  version should win.
</div>

<div class="note-box">
  Fuel bought on the carrier's card is recorded against the settlement so the balance reconciles, but
  it is <strong>not</strong> counted as an expense — you already enter the fuel receipts yourself, and
  counting both would double your largest cost.
</div>
